{"time_unix": 1794350207.5815797, "event": "candidate_created", "payload": {"id": "c1-shared-store-r5", "parent": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "parent_commit": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "parent_candidate": null, "generation": 1, "baseline_commit": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "brief_id": "brief-000001-04ef230e0bee", "worktree": "worktrees/codex-compress-lib-r5-2026-11-10/c1-shared-store-r5", "status": "active", "hypothesis": "Extracting codec CPU contexts and zsmalloc storage into a page_compress library can preserve existing ZSwap frontend ownership, charging, lifecycle and compressed roundtrip behavior while providing a reusable page/object mechanism for subsequent independent XSwap.", "created_unix": 1794350207.580823, "protocol_sha256": "b0116802875e4213260f0e2b07a923e8dfd924a247f73f31d24991e3ecd464de", "mechanism": {"kind": "reviewed_structure", "claim": "ZSwap delegates pool/context and handle store/load/free operations to page_compress while retaining its entry layout, refs, indexes, admission, LRU and memcg policy; one common implementation serves future frontends without per-object wrapper allocations.", "falsifier": "Reject on ownership or accounting drift, non-exercised compression, failed lifecycle/error/configuration coverage, increased per-object/context footprint, or calibrated swap-in/metadata guard regression."}}}
